Multi-threaded PLE n-gram gather, 3-pass QSA select, and granular profile markers

1. Parallelizes host PLE n-gram gather (`Gather.main` in `cuda_batch_state.zig`) across
   8 CPU threads for prompt chunks >= 512 rows, cutting `ple` GPU stall from 155.7 ms ->
   16.6 ms on 16K prefill and 35.2 ms -> 9.3 ms on 245K prefill (100% bit-exact).
2. Upgrades `fn_qsa_select_body` (`flashnext_batch.cu`) from 4-pass 8-bit radix to 3-pass
   11+11+10-bit radix with `__match_any_sync` warp-aggregated SMEM atomics, cutting 245K
   `qsa_select` from 69.4 ms -> 64.5 ms (100% bit-exact).
3. Adds granular `attn_sub` (prep/pool/score/select/core/gate) and `exp_prompt`
   (routed4/shared6) timing lines under `TF_FLASHNEXT_PROFILE=1`.

